## 1. TECHNOLOGY & ERA PROGRESSION SYSTEM

### 1.1 Fix the Era-Regression Loop (CRITICAL - R-001/R-002)

**Current Problem:**
- Technology caps at ~31
- 181 dark ages subtract technology
- Civilisation oscillates Medieval↔Modern permanently
- Zero net progress after day ~1,250

**Proposed Solutions:**

#### Option A: Soft Dark Age Model
```
CURRENT:  dark_age → tech -= N (subtractive, can undo progress)
PROPOSED: dark_age → tech_growth_rate *= 0.3 for DURATION (rate-limited)

Implementation:
- Dark ages no longer DELETE technology
- Instead, they suppress innovation rate for a duration
- Previously researched techs remain known
- Recovery period scales with dark age severity
```

#### Option B: Era Floor Locking
```
CURRENT:  dark_age → era = era - 1 (can regress multiple eras)
PROPOSED: dark_age → era = max(era - 1, FLOOR_ERA)
         where FLOOR_ERA = highest era ever achieved - 1

Implementation:
- Civilisation can only regress ONE era below peak
- Prevents Medieval→Stone Age cascades
- "Institutional memory" preserves some progress
```

#### Option C: Progressive Dark Age Resistance
```
PROPOSED: Each era reached permanently reduces dark_age_trigger_threshold

ERA           | Dark Age Base Threshold | Reduction
--------------|-------------------------|------------
Stone Age     | 100                     | 0%
Tribal        | 95                      | 5%
Early Agric.  | 85                      | 15%
Iron Age      | 70                      | 30%
Medieval      | 50                      | 50%
Modern        | 30                      | 70%
Early Modern  | 15                      | 85%
Industrial    | 5                       | 95%

Implementation:
- Higher eras = more institutional resilience
- Dark ages become rarer as civilisation advances
- Prevents the endless oscillation loop
```

#### Option D: Conditional Regression (RECOMMENDED)
```
COMBINE: B + C

1. Era floor = max_era_achieved - 1 (can only drop one era)
2. Dark age probability scales inversely with:
   - Current era level
   - Treaty stability (treaties_last_100_days / wars_last_100_days)
   - Population stability (pop_variance_last_500_days)
   - Specialist ratio (specialists / population)

3. Technology loss on dark age:
   - 0% tech lost if dark_age_resistance > 70%
   - Scaled loss: tech_lost = (1 - resistance) * base_loss
```

