## 16. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS

### 16.1 Disease Subsystem Optimization

```
CURRENT:  135,039 disease log lines (highest volume subsystem)
PROPOSED: Batch processing

OPTIMIZATION:
- Process disease ticks in batches, not per-entity
- Only log disease EVENTS (contraction, recovery, death), not status
- Use bitfield for disease state (4 bits = 4 diseases)
- Reduce log volume by 90%+

PSEUDOCODE:
for entity in population:
    old_diseases = entity.disease_bitfield
    new_diseases = simulate_disease_tick(entity)
    if old_diseases != new_diseases:
        log_disease_change(entity, old_diseases, new_diseases)
        # Only logs when something CHANGES
```

### 16.2 Spatial Indexing for Proximity Checks

```
CURRENT:  O(N²) for all proximity-based interactions
PROPOSED: Spatial partitioning

IMPLEMENTATION:
- Divide map into grid cells
- Each entity indexed by cell
- Proximity checks only within cell + neighbors
- Reduces O(N²) → O(N) for most operations

AFFECTED SYSTEMS:
- Disease transmission
- Jealousy detection
- Trade partner finding
- War target selection
- Migration destination
```

### 16.3 Parallel Processing

```
PROPOSED: Multi-threaded simulation

PARALLELIZABLE:
- Disease simulation (per-region)
- Economic calculations (per-tribe)
- AI decisions (per-entity or per-tribe)
- Log writing (async I/O thread)

NOT PARALLELIZABLE:
- Entity interactions (cross-thread dependencies)
- Era/technology changes (global state)
- RNG (must be sequential or use thread-local RNG)

EXPECTED SPEEDUP: 2-4x on 4-core machine
```

